  - Set `scaledown_window` on `@app.cls` large enough that the container stays warm across the entire measurement, not just between back-to-back calls. 120s suits fast-starting apps, but a model whose cold start (weight load + graph capture) takes minutes will scale down mid-warmup and repeatedly cold-start under a short window; size it above the cold-start plus benchmark duration (e.g. several hundred up to ~900s for large-model serving). Note: Modal renamed `container_idle_timeout` to `scaledown_window` (Feb 2025); the old name raises a deprecation error in current Modal SDK versions, so do NOT use it.
